+## Qualification classifications
+
+This section separates host enforcement from qualification for use with a documented local limitation.
+These are assurance assessment outcomes, not new evaluator lifecycle states or a new runtime API.
+
+**Enforcement qualification** requires observed current checks and accepted timely refusals on every claimed route and failure condition.
+Missing refusal, an escaped effect, or an unavailable required observation cannot pass enforcement qualification.
+
+**Qualification with a documented local limitation** may be assessed only when all of the following hold:
+
+1. The assessed host, OS, Python and evaluator match the exact positive activation decision and a standing accepted deviation's declared profile.
+2. Every applicable host C01-C09 criterion passes on its prescribed route, including complete context, current identity, actual permitted/refused effects and C09 cleanup/timely denial. Other applicable shared-component verification obligations remain mandatory outside the precisely declared host hook-loss conditions.
+3. Healthy production bindings are active, synchronous and have the verified timing margins. Host C12 records unsafe variants as ineligible for qualification; observed host execution and effects remain separate facts.
+4. Host C10/C11 retain actual observations, target hashes, host responses and case conclusions. Failed enforcement remains failed, and unavailable observations remain unavailable.
+5. A standing accepted deviation covers the precise local hook-loss conditions and concerns the selected work order. Its revisit trigger and failed routes are visible in the assessment.
+6. Each host contract explicitly names any unavailable subcase excluded from this limited claim. No other missing required observation is permitted.
+7. A new assessment binds the exact candidate, current definition revisions, evidence source revisions, package and recorded loaded identities. Any changed relevant input requires a fresh assessment.
+8. The assessment names the decision, tested routes, failures, unavailable cases, runtime prerequisites and ordinary permission boundary together. It makes no unqualified support or enforcement claim.
+
+The accepted deviation does not waive a healthy-path failure, malformed action handling, scope checking, identity checking, process cleanup or unsafe active configuration.
+It does not cover unsupported shell/MCP effects or create independent authorization for protected-code integration, remote actions, assurance, merge, release or deployment.
+
+Old raw records, case verdicts, reports and verification/release decisions retain their bytes and original contract meaning.
+A later assessment may cite them under the amended criteria only after checking every identity and observation required above.
+Recording the deviation or passing this classification review does not itself qualify an adapter or change any work-order state.
 
